// Precomputed particle target coordinates for the five reference
// illustrations (Eye, Flower, Bird, Whale, Milky Way Galaxy), generated
// offline via variable-density blue-noise (Poisson-disk-style)
// sampling: points are proposed weighted by the artwork's own
// dark/light and detail distribution, then accepted only if they clear
// a minimum distance from every already-placed point (smaller in
// dense/detailed regions, larger in faint ones). That minimum-distance
// rejection — not just weighted density — is what gives the result
// even, non-overlapping spacing instead of random clumping.
//
// Each entry: `aspect` is the illustration's content-bounding-box
// width/height (used to fit it into the canvas without distortion —
// see fitIllustration in compositions.js), and `points` is a flat
// [x0,y0,x1,y1,...] array normalized to that bounding box, pre-shuffled
// so the first N*2 values are themselves a valid representative
// subsample for any particle count up to the full pool.

